+## 9. Class group, support genus, and finiteness
+
+The class-group injection is confirmed.  For `Y=X-H` and
+`U=Y-Supp(R_X)`, the dominant first leg gives
+
+```text
+O(Y)^*=O(U)^*=C^*.
+```
+
+The divisor localization sequence injects the free group on reduced
+nonexceptional ramification primes into `Cl(Y)` (`RA:149-160`, `CI:300-305`).
+Therefore any nontrivial relation
+
+```text
+sum q_j C_j + sum q_k Z_k ~ cA + exceptional
+```
+
+is impossible after pushdown to `X` and restriction to `Y`, because `A=H`
+becomes trivial on `Y` and exceptional divisors push down to codimension two.
+The coefficients `nu_k` do not enter this reduced-prime independence test.
