+## 5. Reduced-`H` energy
+
+No ADE point lies on `H` away from `p_0`.  At an ADE point of reduced `H`,
+
+```text
+delta_p(H)=h^t a/2+sum delta(H')
+```
+
+is positive if the point lies on `H`, while the F5 curve is smooth away from
+`p_0` (`P:384-395`, `D9:221-260`).
+
+For
+
+```text
+D_H=Supp(r^*H),        W_H=r^*H-D_H=sum(h_i-1)E_i,
+```
+
+connectedness and adjunction give
+
+```text
+p_a(D_H)=2-(1/2)sum_trees (h-1)^t C(h-1)>=0.
+```
+
+At the unique F5 tree, `sum a_i=3` and `1^t C 1=2`, so
+
+```text
+(h-1)^t C(h-1)=h^t a-2sum a_i+2=q-4.
+```
+
+Thus a `q=6` point consumes two units and a `q=8` point consumes all four
+units of the global reduced-`H` energy (`P:396-423`).  This does not constrain
+affine ADE trees off `H`.
