+## 8. Residual caps and target-image identity
+
+The actual-fibre residual identity is confirmed.  For one scheme fibre
+
+```text
+F_t=Gamma+sum beta_iE_i,
+```
+
+remove every nonexceptional fibre component common with strict ramification,
+with its Cartier ramification coefficient, and write the residual strict
+ramification as `R_o`.  Total-fibre orthogonality gives
+
+```text
+4=Gamma.R_o+beta^t(n-v),        beta^t(n-v)<=4.
+```
+
+The `beta` weights remain present.  This is a cap on one actual fibre after
+common carriers are removed, not a per-singularity cap on raw `n`
+(`P:553-587`, `CI:247-270`).
+
+The producer's target-image cap `P:589-609` is the main mathematical failure
+if read without the coordinator repair.  A generic target line through
+`q=pi(Z_k)` cannot avoid `Z_k`; every such line contains that contracted
+source curve in its pullback, possibly with a pullback multiplicity
+`lambda_k`.
+
+The coordinator's repaired formula is correct.  Let
+
+```text
+D=(pi o r)^*line_q = G_q + ell E,
+R=r^*R_X=R_str+mE,
+R_str=R_(o,q)+V_q,
+V_q=sum_(pi(Z_k)=q) nu_k Z_k,
+v=V_q.E,        n=R_str.E=Cm.
+```
+
+Here `G_q` is the complete nonexceptional part of the line pullback, including
+any `lambda_k Z_k` over `q`.  Orthogonality to the exceptional curves gives
+the usual total-transform identity
+
+```text
+D.R=G_q.R_str+ell^t n.
+```
+
+Since every component of `V_q` is contracted by `pi` to the point on the
+target line, the pulled-back line has zero intersection with `V_q`:
+
+```text
+0=D.V_q=G_q.V_q+ell^t v.
+```
+
+Substituting `R_str=R_(o,q)+V_q` cancels all common-carrier self-intersection
+terms, including the terms involving the unknown `lambda_k`, and gives
+
+```text
+8=G_q.R_(o,q)+sum_(p over q) (ell^(p))^t(n^(p)-v^(p)).
+```
+
+Thus the residual cap is
+
+```text
+sum_(p over q) sum_i (n_i^(p)-v_i^(p)) <= 8.
+```
+
+No `min(lambda_k,nu_k)` term is needed.  The `lambda_k` values are absorbed in
+`G_q`, and the cancellation uses `D.V_q=0` with `V_q` weighted by the
+ramification coefficients `nu_k`.  The raw cap `sum n_i<=8` is valid only in
+the subcell `V_q=0` (`CI:272-298`).
+
+For the generic line wording, the safe statement is that the line is not equal
+to a divisorial ramification image and avoids other contracted target points;
+it need not be disjoint from branch curves, whose intersections are proper
+and included in `G_q.R_(o,q)`.
