+## 9. Class group, support genus, and finiteness
+
+The class-group injection is confirmed.  For `Y=X-H` and
+`U=Y-Supp(R_X)`, the dominant first leg gives
+
+```text
+O(Y)^*=O(U)^*=C^*.
+```
+
+The divisor localization sequence injects the free group on reduced
+nonexceptional ramification primes into `Cl(Y)` (`RA:149-160`, `CI:300-305`).
+Therefore any nontrivial relation
+
+```text
+sum q_j C_j + sum q_k Z_k ~ cA + exceptional
+```
+
+is impossible after pushdown to `X` and restriction to `Y`, because `A=H`
+becomes trivial on `Y` and exceptional divisors push down to codimension two.
+The coefficients `nu_k` do not enter this reduced-prime independence test.
+
+The support-genus identity is also confirmed.  With
+
+```text
+D_R=Supp(r^*R_X),
+W_R=r^*R_X-D_R=sum_k(nu_k-1)Z_k+sum_alpha(m_alpha-1)E_alpha,
+```
+
+one has `p_a(r^*R_X)=9`, `r^*R_X.Z_k=K.Z_k=1`, and both classes are
+orthogonal to exceptional curves.  Adjunction gives
+
+```text
+p_a(D_R)=9+(W_R^2-3sum_k(nu_k-1))/2>=0.
+```
+
+Only in the subcell `nu_k=1` for every contracted carrier does this reduce to
+the exceptional energy bound
+
+```text
+sum_trees (m-1)^t C(m-1)<=18.
+```
+
+There is no theorem in scope forcing that subcell (`P:630-661`,
+`CI:307-327`).
+
+The finite state proof survives without the invalid raw target cap.  There
+are only nine blowup coordinates and finitely many marked root/fibre
+subsystems.  The degree equation bounds the number of horizontal primes,
+their `B`-degrees, and every `nu_k` by four.  Pushing the effective class
+decomposition to `F_2` bounds each nonnegative fibre coefficient by the fixed
+coefficient eleven in `4S_0+11F-2sum E_i`.  With `1<=A.C_j<=8`, the class
+equation and rational adjunction bound all centre multiplicities.  The raw
+contracted carrier classes are finite and at most two can coexist.  Once the
+strict carrier classes and root classes are selected, `n=R_str.E` is
+determined and `m=C^{-1}n` is unique.  Equivalently, the repaired residual
+target cap bounds `n-v`, while the finite carrier list and `nu_k<=4` bound
+`v` (`CI:328-341`).
+
+This is finiteness of discrete numerical classes, target-label partitions,
+proximity graphs, and physical contact partitions.  It is not finiteness of
+coordinates, blowup locations, analytic germs, or moduli.
