+This confirms `P:165-228` against `NS:138-203`.
+
+In the smooth `p_0` row, `S` meets `L`, so the other `B_1` component is the
+contracted one and
+
+```text
+L=F-E_l,
+T=S_0+4F-sum_(i!=l)E_i.
+```
+
+The fibre is exactly `B_1`: any adjacent root would put an ADE point on `H`,
+which is excluded in the smooth case and by the no-other-ADE-on-`H` argument
+below (`P:253-264`).
+
+In the singular row, `L` is a vertical `(-1)` curve disjoint from `S`, so it
+may be the first contraction; in the inverse sequence it is last-created and
+has class
+
+```text
+L=E_l.
+```
+
+Writing `T=S_0+bF-sum_(i in I)E_i`, the section square gives `|I|=2b`.  If
+`h_S` is the coefficient of the retained weight-one exceptional component,
+comparison of
+
+```text
+A=L+S+T+Z_H
+```
+
+gives
+
+```text
+b=5-h_S,
+l notin I,
+Z_H=h_SF-2E_l-sum_(i notin I, i!=l)E_i.
+```
+
+Since `S.T=b-2=3-h_S`, the `q=6/8` result forces
+
+```text
+q=6: h_S=2, T=S_0+3F-sum_(i in I_6)E_i, |I_6|=6,
+     Z_H=2F-2E_l-E_j-E_k;
+
+q=8: h_S=3, T=S_0+2F-sum_(i in I_4)E_i, |I_4|=4,
+     Z_H=3F-2E_l-E_j-E_k-E_u-E_v.
+```
+
+Their squares are `-6` and `-8`, as required.  The retained root has class
+`C_S=F-E_i-E_j`, possibly with successive centres, and
+`T.C_S=1-1_(i in I)-1_(j in I)`, giving exactly the proximity test in
+`P:315-335`.  These class and proximity equations are necessary data; they
+are not effectivity.
+
+## 4. Physical tags and Euler
+
+The F5 bridge supplies the local Cartier list with `sum a_i=3` and
+`h^t a<=8` (`FB:147-209`).  The connected-type theorem supplies only
+`A1,...,A8` and `D4,...,D9` as connected embedded types (`AD:41-69`).  A
+scratch exact rational replay reproduces the allowed `A` and `D` rows before
+the ambient `D9` cutoff; the apparent local `A9` continuation is not a tag
+because `A9` is not an embedded connected type in `D9`.
+
+Putting the actual nonexceptional fibre marking back in is essential
+(`D9:186-219`):
+
+```text
+Before Euler:
+q=6: B_3/A_2, U_3/A_3;
+q=8: B_5/A_4, B_6/A_5, B_7/A_6, B_8/A_7, B_9/A_8,
+     U_5/D_5, U_6/D_6.
+```
+
+The deaths and survivals are as follows.
+
+* `B_4/A_3` and all higher balanced `q=6` `B` rows die because `L` is forced
+  to the endpoint adjacent to the nonexceptional carrier, while the singleton
+  in `2e_1+e_(r-1)` is not that endpoint for `r>=3`.
+* `U_3/A_3` survives because the actual `U_3` marking puts `L` on the central
+  vertex and lets `S,T` share one spin point.
+* `U_4/D_4` dies because its `q=6` vector gives the two section contacts on
+  distinct spins, hence `S.T=0`, contradicting the required `S.T=1`.
+* The `q=8` repeated coefficient cases, for example `A_4` and `D_5`, survive
+  as necessary rows because coefficient two means two distinct physical
+  smooth points on one exceptional component, not a tangent or one doubled
+  germ.
+
+This confirms `P:337-362` and `CI:127-143`.
+
+The producer sentence at `P:364-366` is literally wrong for `q=6`.  Replace
+"the three prescribed smooth attachment points" by:
+
+```text
+the three unit branch attachments, partitioned into two physical smooth
+points for q=6 and three physical smooth points for q=8.
+```
+
+The binding Euler theorem applies to the open
+`U=X minus Supp(H+R_X)` with an actual charged dominant `A2->U` map
+(`EU:46-95`).  It gives
+
+```text
+e(U)=12-r-c,      r+c<=11,
+F5 scope: r+k<=8,
+P1 base for the A1-ruling: r+k<=7.
+```
+
+Here `r=r_0+r_aff` and `k` counts distinct reduced nonexceptional
+ramification primes, independent of their Cartier multiplicities
+(`EU:122-195`).  Every singular F5 state has `k>=1`, so `B_9/A_8` with
+`r_0=8` is impossible.  The `B_8/A_7` cell is extremal:
+
+```text
+r_0=7 => r_aff+k<=1 => r_aff=0 and k=1.
+```
+
+The sole ramification prime must be noncontracted, because a contracted
+affine source line is disjoint from `H` and cannot supply the strict
+attachment at `p_0`; hence its `A`-degree is eight.  Equality also forces
+base `A1` for the new adapted ruling and irreducible reduced support in every
+new-ruling fibre (`EU:197-235`, `CI:172-187`).  These conclusions concern the
+new adapted `A1` ruling, not the original conic `B`-fibration.
+
+## 5. Reduced-`H` energy
+
+No ADE point lies on `H` away from `p_0`.  At an ADE point of reduced `H`,
+
+```text
+delta_p(H)=h^t a/2+sum delta(H')
+```
+
+is positive if the point lies on `H`, while the F5 curve is smooth away from
+`p_0` (`P:384-395`, `D9:221-260`).
+
+For
+
+```text
+D_H=Supp(r^*H),        W_H=r^*H-D_H=sum(h_i-1)E_i,
+```
+
+connectedness and adjunction give
+
+```text
+p_a(D_H)=2-(1/2)sum_trees (h-1)^t C(h-1)>=0.
+```
+
+At the unique F5 tree, `sum a_i=3` and `1^t C 1=2`, so
+
+```text
+(h-1)^t C(h-1)=h^t a-2sum a_i+2=q-4.
+```
+
+Thus a `q=6` point consumes two units and a `q=8` point consumes all four
+units of the global reduced-`H` energy (`P:396-423`).  This does not constrain
+affine ADE trees off `H`.
+
+## 6. Contracted carriers and compatibility
+
+For a nonexceptional curve contracted by `pi` to an affine coefficient
+basepoint, the incidence fibre is the source line over that target point:
+
+```text
+A.Z=0,        B.Z=1.
+```
+
+Adjunction gives `Z^2=-3`, and finiteness near `H` makes it disjoint from
+`S_0`.  In the `F_2` basis,
+
+```text
+Z_J=S_0+2F-sum_(j in J)E_j,        |J|=5.
+```
+
+This confirms `P:425-444`; proximity and effectivity are still additional
+conditions.
+
+The sentence `P:462-463` claiming that three arbitrary five-subsets with
+pairwise intersection two cannot coexist is false.  The corrigendum's
+state-specific repair is correct:
+
+```text
+state      vertices   compatible unordered pairs   clique number
+smooth        70                 560                    2
+q=6           20                  10                    2
+q=8           24                  36                    2
+```
+
+The replay over the finite graphs gives zero compatible triangles in all
+three rows.  The reasons are exactly those in `C:78-177`: all smooth
+candidates contain `l`; all `q=6` candidates contain the fixed outside
+two-set and need complementary three-subsets in `I_6`; `q=8` compatibility
+forces complementary two-subsets in `I_4`, so three cannot occur.  The
+conclusion is only:
+
+```text
+every effective family has at most two contracted carriers.
+```
+
+It is not safe to assert that any vertex or compatible pair is effective.
+The corrigendum line `C:42-46` is safe only as a statement that the five-set
+correction changes no class or energy formula by itself; it must not be read
+as a defense of the producer's later raw target-image cap.
+
+## 7. Ramification class and degrees
+
+The normal-singular incidence integration identifies the resolved source
+different with the Cartier pullback `r^*R_X~2A+B`, connected and containing
+every exceptional curve (`NS:205-263`).  In the `F_2` marking,
+
+```text
+r^*R_X=2A+B=4S_0+11F-2sum_i E_i.
+```
+
+Separate strict nonexceptional ramification into noncontracted divisorial
+primes `C_j`, contracted affine primes `Z_k`, and the actual ADE exceptional
+cycle `M=sum m_alpha E_alpha`.  The fixed-sheet theorem applies only over a
+target divisor: in degree three a ramified divisorial branch has an
+unramified sheet plus one tame transposition, so its different coefficient is
+one (`GB:47-64`).  It does not control a curve mapped to a target point.
+
+The binding equations are therefore
+
+```text
+sum_j C_j+sum_k nu_k Z_k+M
+    =4S_0+11F-2sum_i E_i,
+
+sum_j A.C_j=8,
+sum_j B.C_j+sum_k nu_k=4,
+nu_k>=1.
+```
+
+In particular `nu_k<=4`, but multiplicity one is not proved for contracted
+primes.  At each ADE tree `n=Cm>=0`, with `m>0`, and `M` must be computed in
+the actual root classes, not by assigning the same coefficients to the
+orthogonal total-transform symbols (`P:473-527`, `AD:70-169`).
+
+For a smooth F5 point, the local different has two reduced smooth branches
+with exact boundary totals five and three (`LD:77-158`).  They cannot be one
+global prime without making a rational-forest cycle (`LD:160-190`), so the
+global decomposition has distinct `A`-degrees `3` and `5`.  For singular
+`p_0`, no analogous split is licensed; only a positive partition of eight
+among noncontracted strict primes is known.
+
+Distinct noncontracted `C_j` must have distinct target divisorial images and
+map generically birationally to them; otherwise the degree-three fibre
+accounting with the fixed sheet is exceeded.  This should remain explicit in
+the promoted state.
+
+## 8. Residual caps and target-image identity
+
+The actual-fibre residual identity is confirmed.  For one scheme fibre
+
+```text
+F_t=Gamma+sum beta_iE_i,
+```
+
+remove every nonexceptional fibre component common with strict ramification,
+with its Cartier ramification coefficient, and write the residual strict
+ramification as `R_o`.  Total-fibre orthogonality gives
+
+```text
+4=Gamma.R_o+beta^t(n-v),        beta^t(n-v)<=4.
+```
+
+The `beta` weights remain present.  This is a cap on one actual fibre after
+common carriers are removed, not a per-singularity cap on raw `n`
+(`P:553-587`, `CI:247-270`).
+
+The producer's target-image cap `P:589-609` is the main mathematical failure
+if read without the coordinator repair.  A generic target line through
+`q=pi(Z_k)` cannot avoid `Z_k`; every such line contains that contracted
+source curve in its pullback, possibly with a pullback multiplicity
+`lambda_k`.
+
+The coordinator's repaired formula is correct.  Let
+
+```text
+D=(pi o r)^*line_q = G_q + ell E,
+R=r^*R_X=R_str+mE,
+R_str=R_(o,q)+V_q,
+V_q=sum_(pi(Z_k)=q) nu_k Z_k,
+v=V_q.E,        n=R_str.E=Cm.
+```
+
+Here `G_q` is the complete nonexceptional part of the line pullback, including
+any `lambda_k Z_k` over `q`.  Orthogonality to the exceptional curves gives
+the usual total-transform identity
+
+```text
+D.R=G_q.R_str+ell^t n.
+```
+
+Since every component of `V_q` is contracted by `pi` to the point on the
+target line, the pulled-back line has zero intersection with `V_q`:
+
+```text
+0=D.V_q=G_q.V_q+ell^t v.
+```
+
+Substituting `R_str=R_(o,q)+V_q` cancels all common-carrier self-intersection
+terms, including the terms involving the unknown `lambda_k`, and gives
+
+```text
+8=G_q.R_(o,q)+sum_(p over q) (ell^(p))^t(n^(p)-v^(p)).
+```
+
+Thus the residual cap is
+
+```text
+sum_(p over q) sum_i (n_i^(p)-v_i^(p)) <= 8.
+```
+
+No `min(lambda_k,nu_k)` term is needed.  The `lambda_k` values are absorbed in
+`G_q`, and the cancellation uses `D.V_q=0` with `V_q` weighted by the
+ramification coefficients `nu_k`.  The raw cap `sum n_i<=8` is valid only in
+the subcell `V_q=0` (`CI:272-298`).
+
+For the generic line wording, the safe statement is that the line is not equal
+to a divisorial ramification image and avoids other contracted target points;
+it need not be disjoint from branch curves, whose intersections are proper
+and included in `G_q.R_(o,q)`.
+
+## 9. Class group, support genus, and finiteness
+
+The class-group injection is confirmed.  For `Y=X-H` and
+`U=Y-Supp(R_X)`, the dominant first leg gives
+
+```text
+O(Y)^*=O(U)^*=C^*.
+```
+
+The divisor localization sequence injects the free group on reduced
+nonexceptional ramification primes into `Cl(Y)` (`RA:149-160`, `CI:300-305`).
+Therefore any nontrivial relation
+
+```text
+sum q_j C_j + sum q_k Z_k ~ cA + exceptional
+```
+
+is impossible after pushdown to `X` and restriction to `Y`, because `A=H`
+becomes trivial on `Y` and exceptional divisors push down to codimension two.
+The coefficients `nu_k` do not enter this reduced-prime independence test.
+
+The support-genus identity is also confirmed.  With
+
+```text
+D_R=Supp(r^*R_X),
+W_R=r^*R_X-D_R=sum_k(nu_k-1)Z_k+sum_alpha(m_alpha-1)E_alpha,
+```
+
+one has `p_a(r^*R_X)=9`, `r^*R_X.Z_k=K.Z_k=1`, and both classes are
+orthogonal to exceptional curves.  Adjunction gives
+
+```text
+p_a(D_R)=9+(W_R^2-3sum_k(nu_k-1))/2>=0.
+```
+
+Only in the subcell `nu_k=1` for every contracted carrier does this reduce to
+the exceptional energy bound
+
+```text
+sum_trees (m-1)^t C(m-1)<=18.
+```
+
+There is no theorem in scope forcing that subcell (`P:630-661`,
+`CI:307-327`).
+
+The finite state proof survives without the invalid raw target cap.  There
+are only nine blowup coordinates and finitely many marked root/fibre
+subsystems.  The degree equation bounds the number of horizontal primes,
+their `B`-degrees, and every `nu_k` by four.  Pushing the effective class
+decomposition to `F_2` bounds each nonnegative fibre coefficient by the fixed
+coefficient eleven in `4S_0+11F-2sum E_i`.  With `1<=A.C_j<=8`, the class
+equation and rational adjunction bound all centre multiplicities.  The raw
+contracted carrier classes are finite and at most two can coexist.  Once the
+strict carrier classes and root classes are selected, `n=R_str.E` is
+determined and `m=C^{-1}n` is unique.  Equivalently, the repaired residual
+target cap bounds `n-v`, while the finite carrier list and `nu_k<=4` bound
+`v` (`CI:328-341`).
+
+This is finiteness of discrete numerical classes, target-label partitions,
+proximity graphs, and physical contact partitions.  It is not finiteness of
+coordinates, blowup locations, analytic germs, or moduli.
+
