+## 11. Maximum safe theorem
+
+In the charged normal irreducible class-`2A+3B`, reduced-infinity,
+finite-near-`H`, dominant-first-leg scope, the infinity curve is F5 and all
+eight `H.R_X` units occur at its unique triple/tangency point.  After choosing
+one section branch `S`, the minimal resolution has an `S`-adapted nine-blowup
+marking over `F_2`:
+
+```text
+S=S_0,        B=F,        A=2S_0+5F-sum E_i.
+```
+
+The smooth state has
+
+```text
+L=F-E_l,      T=S_0+4F-sum_(i!=l)E_i
+```
+
+and the smooth local different splits into two distinct global ramification
+primes of `A`-degrees `3` and `5`.
+
+Before Euler, the singular local necessary tags are exactly
+
+```text
+B_3/A_2, U_3/A_3,
+B_5/A_4, B_6/A_5, B_7/A_6, B_8/A_7, B_9/A_8,
+U_5/D_5, U_6/D_6.
+```
+
+For singular tags, `L=E_l`, the total-transform classes and proximity rules in
+Section 3 are binding, and the physical attachment partition is part of the
+state.  The Euler theorem eliminates `B_9/A_8`, leaving eight singular tags
+plus the smooth row.  The `B_8/A_7` row is extremal with
+`r_aff=0`, `k=1`, one noncontracted strict prime of `A`-degree eight, and the
+new adapted `A1`-ruling equality conditions.
+
+Every affine coefficient-basepoint carrier has class
+
+```text
+Z_J=S_0+2F-sum_(j in J)E_j,        |J|=5,
+```
+
+with raw marked compatibility graph counts `(70,560)`, `(20,10)`, and
+`(24,36)`, each of clique number two.  Hence an effective configuration has
+at most two such carriers, but no vertex or edge is asserted effective.
+
+Ramification satisfies
+
+```text
+sum_j C_j+sum_k nu_k Z_k+M=4S_0+11F-2sum E_i,
+sum_j A.C_j=8,
+sum_j B.C_j+sum_k nu_k=4,
+1<=nu_k<=4.
+```
+
+Noncontracted divisorial primes have coefficient one.  Contracted affine
+primes have uncontrolled positive coefficients `nu_k`.  The actual-fibre cap,
+the residual target-image cap, the class-group injection, and support-genus
+identity above are binding.  The ramification-energy cap eighteen is
+conditional on all `nu_k=1`.
+
+This theorem is only a finite necessary numerical/combinatorial threat state.
+It proves no effectivity of tags, root embeddings, subset classes, proximity
+histories, physical contact partitions, equality cells, carrier decompositions,
+analytic germs, coefficient tuples, finite cubic algebras, polynomial maps,
+counterexamples, or JC2.
